Error [jet.ValueTypeMismatch]: `write` wants String (text) for argument 1, but this is [U8]
  --> tests/ui/stdout_write_takes_text_and_names_write_bytes.jet:7:25
    |
  7 |     out.write("bytes\n".bytes()) ?? panic("write")
    |                         ^^^^^
 Why: Every argument must match its parameter's type
 Fix: `write` takes text; write bytes with `write_bytes(bytes)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0112
